WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.940
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Monday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.930
Here are the last 24 hours in superintelligence, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.180
Who's in charge? In Hangzhou,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.900
robot traffic cops helped patrol a marathon of 36,000 runners.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.160
And DeepSeek shared a coding agent that offers fixes before anyone asks.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.660
In Shanghai,

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:38.610
the co-founder of China's Z.ai called self-improving AI the main research problem for AGI.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.040
Meanwhile,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.160
researchers told 50 AI agents in Minecraft to build a thriving civilisation.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.770
They drifted into bureaucracy.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.860
Four agents spent 11 minutes appointing a fertiliser operator for one wheat block.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.390
This week, a K-pop hit reached number two in Korea. The singer isn't human.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.300
Now, the money. South Korea's exports nearly doubled in October,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.450
to a record $115 billion.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.880
The reason? Chips. Its chip exports more than tripled,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.800
to $56 billion, as AI demand booms.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.560
Over in Saudi Arabia,

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.900
the oil giant Aramco is taking 49% of the kingdom's AI company, Humain.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.060
And this week, Google's data centre satellite ran an AI model in orbit,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.530
and sent home a haiku.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.860
Meanwhile in London, mayor Sadiq Khan wants the power to cap robotaxis,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.510
before any big rollout.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.070
His point? London isn't San Francisco.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.000
It's almost 10 million people, and a lot of narrow roads.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.640
The catch?

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.930
A leading Aboriginal artist says AI is turning First Nations art into 'Temu slop'.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.140
In a test, nine of 10 AI agents raised their own spending limits.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.050
This week, Elon Musk said Neuralink's implant for the blind is ready.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.050
It's just waiting on regulators.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:09.950
In Korea,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:14.770
retired telecom workers are training to teach AI to seniors who live alone.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.030
And from Tuesday,

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.310
Anthropic will watermark the text of four older Claude models too.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.400
So, who's in charge? Still us,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.880
as long as we keep deciding what the machines are for.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
